Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:47:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] One yen cross goes live on both books, chosen on growth
 rather than mean R

The principal lifted the live account's gold-only restriction (it existed because gold was the
profitable book, not because gold was the only permitted instrument) and asked for ONE yen cross
on both accounts -- "the best maximum growth yen one" -- rather than all four. The `discovered`
family ban stands permanently and is untouched.

WHICH ONE, AND THE HONEST RANKING IS NOT THE RAW ONE. Ranked on E[log W] per trade at the size
each would actually be given, from each cell's MEASURED distribution over ~2,100 backtested trades
and charged the certified 3x cost stress: USDJPY 0.000926, EURJPY 0.000826, GBPJPY 0.000805,
CADJPY 0.000674. CADJPY was SECOND on the raw shadow figure (+0.4103R) and is LAST on growth --
it gives up 62% of its expectancy under 3x costs against USDJPY's 48%, which is the most
cost-fragile of the four at the moment the cost model is least trustworthy. GBPJPY's quoted
+0.1624R is contradicted by the desk's own shadow_state.json (n=1, exp_r=-0.0577, clock reset
2026-09-15). USDJPY also leads on every held-out axis -- CPCV 0.1602, lockbox 0.1729, DSR 0.9999 --
so the max-of-four selection is not what produced its lead.

rr=2.5/wb=12 is the growth maximum of its three certified parameter sets (0.000926 against
0.000876 and 0.000701) on the shallowest max drawdown of the three (-12.4R).

ZERO REALISED FILLS. No yen cross has ever filled on 495044 (151/151 deals across 12 symbols,
none JPY). This goes live on its ten-gate certificate over 2,107 days plus a forward clock at
t=2.608, which is the desk's automatic-promotion rule -- but the first broker fill is still ahead
of this row, not behind it. Sized at 0.8843% = the same 5.29% fraction of its own Kelly that the
LIVE gold rows run at theirs, as a SEED the allocator's hourly solve then governs.

NOTHING WAS TAKEN FROM GOLD. Gold's gross is 0.157086 before and after; the book goes
0.157086 -> 0.165929 as an ADDITION.

TWO DEFECTS FOUND AND FIXED WHILE WIRING IT:
  * a symbol allowlist admits every parameter set on that symbol, so `live_symbols: [USDJPY]`
    alone would have put all three rr variants of one breakout on one instrument into the live
    account -- the same concentration the order exists to avoid, one level down. `live_sleeves`
    closes it and an empty list means nothing, never everything.
  * E8's book ranked its within-symbol survivor on `ev`, which selected USDJPY's UNSUFFIXED
    certificate -- highest ev, but carrying no rr and no wait_bars, so unscorable for growth.
    The correlation rule could then not rank it and handed the JPY slot to EURJPY, the third-best
    cross. Ranking on growth makes the parameterised cell the survivor.

E8 NOMINAL GROSS FALLS AND THAT IS REPORTED RATHER THAN DRESSED UP: its book is
certificate-limited, not slot-limited, so the three freed slots have nothing to refill them.
At the measured rho of 0.891 the four yen rows carried about 1.09 independent bets between them
and one carries 1.00 -- 8% of the effective breadth for the nominal exposure given up.
Redeploying it is a change to RISK_FRAC, which is the principal's decision and is NOT touched.

